# ACT ONE

[[Section marker above. The line below is a synopsis marker.]]

= Two flatmates argue over who lost the spare key while a delivery waits at the door.

INT. ROOFTOP FLAT - KITCHEN - NIGHT #1#

[[Scene heading with a scene number. Action follows.]]

A tiny kitchen with a window onto the water tanks. A pressure cooker rattles on the stove. A row of hooks by the door: three hooks, two keys.

NANDINI (20s, apron, flour on one cheek) stares at the empty hook.

ROHAN (20s, headphones round his neck) comes in eating a banana.

[[Character, parenthetical and dialogue.]]

NANDINI
(not turning round)
Where is the spare key?

ROHAN
Which spare key?

NANDINI
The *only* spare key. The one with the **green** tag.

[[Dual dialogue: both speak at the same time.]]

ROHAN
I gave it back to you on Sunday!

NANDINI ^
You did not give it back to me on Sunday!

The DOORBELL rings. They both freeze.

[[A shot, written as an upper-case action line. Fountain has no shot element of its own.]]

CLOSE ON THE PRESSURE COOKER

The whistle blows, long and shrill.

[[Centered text.]]

> TWO MINUTES EARLIER <

[[A forced character cue for a name that is not all capitals, with a character extension.]]

@Delivery Boy (O.S.)
Order for Nandini? I need a signature.

ROHAN
(whispering)
Do not open it. If we open it we have to admit the door was locked from outside.

!NANDINI OPENS IT ANYWAY.

[[Forced action above, so the capitals do not read as a character cue. A page break follows.]]

===

[[After the page break the scene continues. Lyrics come next.]]

Rohan sings to cover the silence, badly.

ROHAN
~Where did you go, little key,
~Did you run away from me

On the doorstep, hanging from the doorbell, is the KEY with the green tag.

/* A cut line we kept in the boneyard:
Rohan claims he planned this all along. */

NANDINI
(holding it up)
_Sunday._

[[Transition.]]

CUT TO:

[[Forced transition.]]

> FADE OUT.
